## Install attempt + error (user report)
Timestamp: 2026-02-04 07:04 UTC

Command (user):
- `sudo apt install pgadmin4-web`

Result:
- `E: Unable to locate package pgadmin4-web`

Interpretation:
- The pgAdmin packages are not in the default Ubuntu apt sources; the pgAdmin APT repository must be added first (repo key + apt source), then `apt update`.

## Fix (generic, should work on Ubuntu)
Timestamp: 2026-02-04 07:04 UTC

1) Confirm your Ubuntu codename:
- `lsb_release -cs`

2) Add pgAdmin repo key + source using the detected codename:
- `CODENAME="$(lsb_release -cs)"`
- `sudo install -d -m 0755 /usr/share/keyrings`
- `curl -fsSL https://apt.postgresql.org/pub/pgadmin/pgadmin4/apt/pgadmin4_pubkey.gpg | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/pgadmin4.gpg`
- `echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/pgadmin4.gpg] https://apt.postgresql.org/pub/pgadmin/pgadmin4/apt/ ${CODENAME} pgadmin4 main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/pgadmin4.list`

3) Update + verify package is now visible:
- `sudo apt update`
- `apt-cache policy pgadmin4-web | sed -n '1,25p'`

4) Install + configure:
- `sudo apt install -y pgadmin4-web`
- `sudo /usr/pgadmin4/bin/setup-web.sh`

If `apt update` shows a 404 for your codename, don’t guess—use the official pgAdmin download page’s “Repository Configuration” block for your distro and rerun using exactly those lines.

